In this subdirectory there's the beginnings of an automated system to
write code for inclusion in gretl_to_python.cpp, gretl_calls.cpp and
gretl_calls.h, via a C program that reads the libgretl headers.

At present the apparatus is only concerned with libgretl functions
that return a MODEL struct -- and it handles only those with a
certain "basic" signature.

Running model_funcs_query.sh exercises the apparatus. The output shows
a regimented version of the model-function signatures that were found,
and in the "basic" cases also shows content intended for inclusion in
the C++ files.
